{
  "understanding": "The selected deployment branch constructs the repository's Paxos implementation, with master-assigned replica identity and initial leader status, per-instance ballots and commands, separate prepare/accept/commit handlers, and an execution loop that requests recovery for stalled instances. The supplied code supports a partial account of decision processing and application, but startup, proposal admission, ballot construction, broadcast selection, transport dispatch, and master-driven leadership changes remain unread. Facts below describe local state and reported metadata; they do not establish agreement, unique quorum participation, durable completion, or client-visible correctness. Constructor defaults enable execution and direct replies and disable durability. Whether later initialization changes these defaults remains unresolved.",
  "audit_spec": {
    "version": 1,
    "target_profile": {
